[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 8 | `hdr_compare` | `((h1[2] ^ h2[2]) & 0x0C) != 0` — sampling-rate bits (bits 2–3) of `h1[2]` differ from `h2[2]`, with rows 1–7 passing | returns `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 9 | `hdr_compare` | `((h1[2] & 0xF0) == 0) != ((h2[2] & 0xF0) == 0)` — exactly one of the two headers has a zero (free-format) bitrate nibble, with rows 1–8 passing | returns `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 10 | `hdr_compare` | `h1 == NULL` **while** `hdr_valid(h2)` is false — legal in C because `&&` short-circuits before `h1` is read | returns `0`, no crash |
