[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 12 | `hdr_compare` | `h1 == h2` (aliasing the same 3 bytes) with a valid header — the `^`/nibble terms all compare a byte with itself | returns `1` (accept), for every valid `h2` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 13 | `hdr_compare` | reading only 3 bytes: `h1[0]` is **never** dereferenced by the C at all (no term mentions `h1[0]`), and neither side may read `h[3]` or beyond | result independent of `h1[0]`; buffers of exactly 3 bytes suffice for both sides |
