[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Mechanical derivation of the axes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The public API (`c_src/include/lib.h`) is one entry point:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m int hdr_compare(const uint8_t *h1, const uint8_t *h2);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is **no** runtime option, mode, flag, setter, context/handle struct, global
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m variable, byte-order switch, or `#ifdef` in the C source — so there are no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "options set" axes. The library is a pure function of the input bytes, and its
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m entire configuration surface is the **shape of the two 3-byte inputs**. `hdr_valid`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m is `static` (not part of the ABI) but is the lowest-level unit of behaviour; it is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exercised *through* `hdr_compare`'s first term, which is the only way an external
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m caller can reach it, so the table drives the real entry point rather than a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m convenience wrapper.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The axes are exactly the sub-expressions the C branches on:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | axis | source expression | distinct classes the C treats differently |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |------|-------------------|-------------------------------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | A. `h2` sync byte | `h2[0] == 0xff` | `0xff` / anything else |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | B. `h2[1]` class | `(h2[1] & 0xF0) == 0xf0` vs `(h2[1] & 0xFE) == 0xe2` | high-nibble class `[0xf0,0xff]` (16) / MPEG-2.5 class `{0xe2,0xe3}` (2) / neither (238) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C. `h2[1]` layer field | `((h2[1] >> 1) & 3)` | `0` (reserved → reject) / `1` / `2` / `3` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | D. `h2[2]` bitrate nibble | `(h2[2] >> 4)` | `15` (reject) / `0` (free format) / `1..14` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | E. `h2[2]` samplerate field | `((h2[2] >> 2) & 3)` | `3` (reserved → reject) / `0` / `1` / `2` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | F. `h1[1]` vs `h2[1]` | `(h1[1] ^ h2[1]) & 0xFE` | equal-except-bit-0 (bit 0 same / bit 0 flipped) / differing in ≥1 masked bit |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | G. `h1[2]` vs `h2[2]` samplerate bits | `(h1[2] ^ h2[2]) & 0x0C` | equal / differing |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | H. free-format nibble agreement | `((h1[2] & 0xF0) == 0) ^ ((h2[2] & 0xF0) == 0)` | both zero / both non-zero / exactly one zero |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | I. pointer shape | which bytes are dereferenced | distinct buffers / aliased (`h1 == h2`) / `h1` unreadable while `h2` invalid (short-circuit) / `h1[0]` arbitrary (never read) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Derived constants (computed from the predicates, used to size the tests):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **14** of 256 `h2[1]` values pass axes B+C — `{e2,e3,f2,f3,f4,f5,f6,f7,fa,fb,fc,fd,fe,ff}`;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **180** of 256 `h2[2]` values pass axes D+E; so **2 520** of 65 536 `h2` tails are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m valid, and for each there are exactly **2** accepting `h1[1]` values and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **16** accepting `h1[2]` values.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Configuration table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Each row is a combination of the axes above that the C distinguishes. Every row is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m driven through the `hdr_compare` export of **both** `.so` files with **many
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m randomized inputs** (fixed seed, SplitMix64) plus the row's boundary values, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the returned `int`s must be byte-identical. Rows 1–4 are the exhaustive sweeps
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m that subsume the cross-product; rows 5–24 are the targeted combinations.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `hdr_compare` | **Exhaustive** over the whole meaningful space: all 2^32 combinations of `(h1[1], h1[2], h2[1], h2[2])` with `h2[0] = 0xff`, split into 256 sharded sub-sweeps | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 | `hdr_compare` | **Exhaustive** over all 256 values of `h2[0]` × all 65 536 `h2[1..3]` tails, with `h1` tail both matching and mismatching (axis A × B × C × D × E) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 3 | `hdr_compare` | **Exhaustive** over all 2^16 `(h1[1], h1[2])` for every one of the 2 520 valid `h2` tails (axes F × G × H under every accepting `h2`) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 4 | `hdr_compare` | **Exhaustive** over all 2^16 `h2` tails for a representative set of `h1` tails, `h2[0] = 0xff` (rejection classes B/C/D/E in full) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 5 | `hdr_compare` | Fully random 5 relevant bytes, uniform (mostly-rejecting mass), 20 M randomized draws | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 6 | `hdr_compare` | Random but *biased to accept*: `h2[0]=0xff`, `h2[1]` drawn from the 14 valid values, `h2[2]` from the 180 valid values, `h1` tail drawn near-matching | [x] |
