[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 8 | `hdr_compare` | Axis A: all 255 non-`0xff` `h2[0]` values with an otherwise perfectly matching valid header → reject | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 9 | `hdr_compare` | Axis B class 1: `h2[1] ∈ [0xf0,0xff]` (all 16), each × all 256 `h2[2]` × matching `h1` | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 10 | `hdr_compare` | Axis B class 2: `h2[1] ∈ {0xe2,0xe3}` (MPEG-2.5 branch, reached only via the `& 0xFE` test) × all 256 `h2[2]` × matching `h1` | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 11 | `hdr_compare` | Axis B class 3: `h2[1]` in neither class (all 238 values) × valid `h2[2]` × matching `h1` | [x] |
